      "attachmentNote": "Galictis cuja. The hamstring field, and the origins are what make it one field: biceps femoris from the dorsal ischial tuberosity, semitendinosus from the ischial tuberosity AND the tail — its caudal belly fleshy from the transverse process of caudal vertebra 2 and aponeurotic from C1 and C3 — semimembranosus from the caudal ramus of the ischium. Ercoli et al. read that RESTRICTED caudal origin as a derived mustelid condition, so the row is scored as C1–C3 rather than as a broad caudal sheet. The caudal-vertebral head is the one worth noting — a thigh muscle taking origin from the tail. Insertions run to the tibia in all three, with semimembranosus also on the medial femoral epicondyle and biceps femoris on the lateral.",
